.TH "XmeNamesAreEqual" "library call"
.nh
.SH "NAME"
\fB\%XmeNamesAreEqual\fP \(em A widget writer function that compares a resource value with a name
.iX "XmeNamesAreEqual"
.iX "Xme functions" "XmeNamesAreEqual"
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.PP
.nf
#include <Xm/XmP\&.h>
\fBBoolean \fBXmeNamesAreEqual\fP\fR(
\fBconst char *\fBin_str\fR\fR,
\fBconst char *\fBtest_str\fR\fR);
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fB\%XmeNamesAreEqual\fP compares the string \fIin_str\fP, without
regard to
case and without a leading \fB\%Xm\fP or \fB\%xm\fP, with
\fItest_str\fP, which must
be in lower case\&.  Resource converters use it to accept
\fB\%XmPIXELS\fP,
\fB\%pixels\fP and \fB\%Pixels\fP alike for the value \fB\%pixels\fP\&.
.IP "\fIin_str\fP" 10
Specifies the string to test\&.
.IP "\fItest_str\fP" 10
Specifies the name, in lower case and without the \fB\%Xm\fP prefix\&.
.PP
Motif 1\&.2 called this function \fB\%_XmStringsAreEqual\fP\&.  The
library still exports that name for old binaries, and
\fB\%<Xm/XmP\&.h>\fP defines it as a macro for \fB\%XmeNamesAreEqual\fP
unless \fB\%NO_XM_1_2_BC\fP is defined; new code should use
\fB\%XmeNamesAreEqual\fP\&.
.SH "RETURN"
.PP
Returns True if the strings are equal, and False otherwise\&.
.SH "RELATED"
.PP
\fB\%XmeParseUnits\fP(3)\&.
